{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Your first father.</b> He is Jeroboam, whom Israel chose as king, not by the word of HaShem." "<b>And your intercessors.</b> They are the princes, intercessors of the king, or the Levites, intercessors of the priests. Some say \"your father\" means teachers, as in \"My father, my father, chariot of Israel\" (2 Kings 2:12), and \"He made me a father to Pharaoh\" (Genesis 45:8), \"the father of all who play the pipe and lyre\" (Genesis 4:21), and the \"intercessors\" are the students, from the root of כי המליץ (Genesis 42:23)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {1 "The third citation, אבי כל תופש כנור, is actually Genesis 4:21, not Genesis 45 as the Hebrew 'שם מ\"ה' appears to indicate; rendered as printed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:51.366477330Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}